I see you're trying to ask me how to create a login form for an interview and inquiry drink glass for staff.

To answer your question, I'll assume you want to know how to create a simple web-based system using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript (or possibly a framework like React or Angular). Here's a high-level overview of the steps:

1. **Create the basic structure**: Start by creating an HTML file with the basic structure for your login form:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Staff Login</title>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Staff Login</h1>
  <form id="login-form">
    <!-- Add input fields for username and password -->
    <label for="username">Username:</label>
    <input type="text" id="username" name="username"><br><br>
    <label for="password">Password:</label>
    <input type="password" id="password" name="password"><br><br>
    <!-- Add a submit button -->
    <button type="submit">Login</button>
  </form>
</body>
</html>
```
2. **Add JavaScript logic**: In the same HTML file, add some basic JavaScript to handle the form submission and validate the input:
```javascript
const loginForm = document.getElementById('login-form');

loginForm.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
  e.preventDefault();

  const username = document.getElementById('username').value;
  const password = document.getElementById('password').value;

  // TO DO: Add authentication logic here (e.g., check against a database or API)
  // For now, just log the input values
  console.log(`Username: ${username}, Password: ${password}`);
});
```
3. **Style the form (optional)**: If you want to add some visual flair to your login form, you can use CSS to style it:
```css
body {
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}

#login-form {
  max-width: 300px;
  margin: 40px auto;
  background-color: #f9f9f9;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  box-shadow: 0px 5px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
}

#login-form label {
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

#login-form input[type="text"], #login-form input[type="password"] {
  width: 100%;
  height: 40px;
  padding: 10px;
  font-size: 16px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
}

#login-form button[type="submit"] {
  background-color: #4CAF50;
  color: #fff;
  padding: 10px 20px;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 5px;
  cursor: pointer;
}
```
This is just a basic example to get you started. You'll need to add more functionality, such as authentication logic and error handling, to make your login form secure and user-friendly.

As for the "inquiry drink glass" part, I'm assuming you want to create a simple form for staff to submit their inquiry or request. You can add another HTML file with a similar structure, and use JavaScript to handle the form submission and send the data to a backend API (if needed).

Please let me know if this helps, or if you have any specific questions about implementing these features!
